  "summary": "Held a year late because of the coronavirus pandemic, the 2021 election saw Labour's Sadiq Khan re-elected for a second term as Mayor of London. Khan led Conservative Shaun Bailey by 40.0% to 35.3% on first preferences and won 55.2% to 44.8% after second preferences were redistributed. Labour remained the largest party on the London Assembly with 11 seats, while the Conservatives rose to 9 and the Greens and Liberal Democrats each gained a seat. This was the final mayoral election held under the Supplementary Vote.",
  "highlights": [
    "Sadiq Khan re-elected for a second term as Mayor of London",
    "Election postponed a year from May 2020 due to the pandemic",
    "Khan beats Shaun Bailey 55.2% to 44.8% after second preferences",
    "Greens win a third Assembly seat — their joint-highest",
    "A record ~114,000 first-preference ballots rejected (5%)",
    "Last mayoral contest under the Supplementary Vote"
  ],
